You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C02
Scenario title: Afternoon Pickup and Caregiver Handover
Initial workflow description:
I arrange who will pick up my child and check that they got home. Sometimes the person collecting them changes during the day.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "Who are the people who may collect your child, and does the childcare provider hold a pre-approved list of authorised collectors that you maintain?",
      "answer": "The people who may collect the child are the partner and a backup caregiver, with the mother arranging things. The provider holds an authorized pickup list, but only the provider (the teacher) updates it — the mother cannot update it directly herself."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "When the pickup person changes during the day, what is the minimum that must happen for the change to be accepted — for example, is a phone call to the provider enough, or is written confirmation required?",
      "answer": "The mother must request the change from the teacher, and the provider must acknowledge it before the changed pickup takes place. The specific form of that acknowledgment (phone call, written message, etc.) is not specified, but collection cannot proceed until the acknowledgment is received."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "Which channel or tool do you currently use to notify the childcare provider and the collector about pickup arrangements or last-minute changes?",
      "answer": "A childcare messaging app is used to communicate with the provider. A shared family calendar is used to coordinate within the household. The specific channel used to notify the collector directly is not specified beyond general confirmation of availability."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How do you confirm that your child has arrived home safely after pickup — what does that confirmation look like and who sends it?",
      "answer": "The partner records a home arrival note in a family handover log after collecting the child. If that confirmation is not logged by the end of the pickup window, the mother follows up with the collector and the teacher."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What do you do if the expected collector has not arrived by a certain time and you cannot reach them — who takes over and what steps are followed?",
      "answer": "If collection has not been confirmed by the end of the pickup window, the mother contacts both the collector and the teacher. Who physically takes over collection in that scenario is not specified beyond that escalation step."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "On a typical week, how many days does the pickup arrangement stay the same versus change, and do changes tend to happen at a particular time of day?",
      "answer": "The workflow runs each scheduled childcare afternoon. The exact number of days the arrangement stays the same versus changes, and the typical time of day when changes occur, are not specified in the available information."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
Return JSON with this shape:
{
  "workflow": {
    "activities": [
